lue from `a` is less than the one from `b`, or `0` otherwise./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_comilt_ss)_mm_comile_ss/// `1` if the value from `a` is less than or equal to the one from `b`, or `0`/// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_comile_ss)_mm_comigt_ss/// `1` if the value from `a` is greater than the one from `b`, or `0`/// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_comigt_ss)_mm_comige_ss/// `1` if the value from `a` is greater than or equal to the one from `b`, or/// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_comige_ss)_mm_comineq_ss/// `1` if they are **not** equal, or `0` otherwise./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_comineq_ss)_mm_ucomieq_ss/// `1` if they are equal, or `0` otherwise. This instruction will not signal/// an exception if either argument is a quiet NaN./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_ucomieq_ss)_mm_ucomilt_ss/// This instruction will not signal an exception if either argument is a quiet/// NaN./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_ucomilt_ss)_mm_ucomile_ss/// otherwise. This instruction will not signal an exception if either argument/// is a quiet NaN./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_ucomile_ss)_mm_ucomigt_ss/// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_ucomigt_ss)_mm_ucomige_ss/// `0` otherwise. This instruction will not signal an exception if either/// argument is a quiet NaN./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_ucomige_ss)_mm_ucomineq_ss/// `1` if they are **not** equal, or `0` otherwise. This instruction will not/// signal an exception if either argument is a quiet NaN./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_ucomineq_ss)_mm_cvtss_si32/// Converts the lowest 32 bit float in the input vector to a 32 bit integer./// The result is rounded according to the current rounding mode. If the result/// cannot be represented as a 32 bit integer the result will be `0x8000_0000`/// (`i32::MIN`)./// This corresponds to the `CVTSS2SI` instruction (with 32 bit output)./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_cvtss_si32)_mm_cvt_ss2si/// Alias for [`_mm_cvtss_si32`](fn._mm_cvtss_si32.html)./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_cvt_ss2si)_mm_cvttss_si32/// Converts the lowest 32 bit float in the input vector to a 32 bit integer/// with/// truncation./// The result is rounded always using truncation (round towards zero). If the/// result cannot be represented as a 32 bit integer the result will be/// `0x8000_0000` (`i32::MIN`)./// This corresponds to the `CVTTSS2SI` instruction (with 32 bit output)./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_cvttss_si32)_mm_cvtt_ss2si/// Alias for [`_mm_cvttss_si32`](fn._mm_cvttss_si32.html)./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_cvtt_ss2si)_mm_cvtss_f32/// Extracts the lowest 32 bit float from the input vector./// [Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_cvtss_f32)// No point in using assert_instrs. In Unix x86_64 calling convention this is a// no-op, and on msvc it's just a `mov`._